OK, my project would be using a small microservice called Doctor, responsible for checking the health of the services.  
However, after some tests (without the Doctor), I noticed that resources were starting to become scarce, so I decided to remove the Doctor service from the project.  

Even though Doctor was a very lightweight service and used Protobufers and gRPC for performance and efficiency, I realized it could be “replaced” by something similar.  

Introducing: KeyDB Health Monitor  

