Points to consider about the problem:

1. The services have a 5s lock, meaning if more than one healthcheck call is made within 5s, the service will reset the timer and count another 5s of lock time.  
2. Because of the lock, if a worker pings the service while it’s locked, the worker will receive a timeout error, and the next worker that pings the service will get another lock, and so on.  

